// Rule: [T1543.002] Spectre - Hardware Monitor Systemd Persistence
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1543.002
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceFileEvents
// Purpose: Campaign-specific hunting for the source observed on Defender-onboarded Linux servers.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceFileEvents for hardware monitor systemd persistence using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceFileEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: SPECTRE execution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// SPECTRE hardware-monitor.service persistence hunt
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Telemetry: DeviceFileEvents from Microsoft Defender for Endpoint on Linux
// Meaning: A match identifies creation/modification/observation of the source-reported
// systemd unit name in a system unit directory. It does not prove SPECTRE execution.
DeviceFileEvents
| where FileName =~ "hardware-monitor.service"
| where FolderPath startswith "/etc/systemd/system/"
    or FolderPath startswith "/usr/lib/systemd/system/"
    or FolderPath startswith "/lib/systemd/system/"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, ActionType, FileName, FolderPath,
          SHA1, FileSize, InitiatingProcessFileName,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessAccountName,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc

